From 7b922bcff4e82966372c95d47ab89686c7dd622d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:16:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] remoteproc: qcom: pas: pass no resource table when the
 firmware has none

qcom_pas_parse_firmware() passes rproc->table_ptr and rproc->table_sz
to qcom_pas_get_rsc_table() even when rproc_elf_load_rsc_table() found
no resource table in the firmware. That only works on the first boot,
when both are still zero. After it, table_sz holds the size of the
table the PAS service returned: stopping the remote processor, or
failing to start it, frees the cached table and clears table_ptr but
leaves table_sz alone. The next start then hands a NULL table with a
non-zero size to the PAS backend. The SCM backend replaces a NULL table
with an empty one, which hides this, but the TEE backend copies from
it. Stopping and starting the CDSP on a QCS8300 board with the TEE PAS
backend:

  remoteproc remoteproc2: powering up cdsp
  pc : __pi_memcpy_generic+0x110/0x22c
  lr : qcom_pas_tee_get_rsc_table+0xf4/0x25c
  Call trace:
   __pi_memcpy_generic+0x110/0x22c (P)
   qcom_pas_get_rsc_table+0x38/0x60
   qcom_pas_parse_firmware+0xa0/0x100
   rproc_boot+0x2d4/0x380
   state_store+0x40/0x100

Use the table from the firmware only when it was found, and pass NULL
and zero otherwise, as the comment in the function already describes.

Fixes: a4584bff63c8 ("remoteproc: pas: Extend parse_fw callback to fetch resources via SMC call")
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index d9cce1206835..f0e33ce40f69 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@ static int qcom_pas_parse_firmware(struct rproc *rproc, const struct firmware *f
 	struct resource_table *table = NULL;
 	size_t output_rt_size;
 	void *output_rt;
-	size_t table_sz;
+	size_t table_sz = 0;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = qcom_register_dump_segments(rproc, fw);
@@ -499,11 +499,12 @@ static int qcom_pas_parse_firmware(struct rproc *rproc, const struct firmware *f
 		return 0;
 
 	ret = rproc_elf_load_rsc_table(rproc, fw);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
 		dev_dbg(&rproc->dev, "Failed to load resource table from firmware\n");
-
-	table = rproc->table_ptr;
-	table_sz = rproc->table_sz;
+	} else {
+		table = rproc->table_ptr;
+		table_sz = rproc->table_sz;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * The resources consumed by Qualcomm remote processors fall into two categories:
-- 
